- FDA complete response letters, U.S. Food and Drug Administration, via the openFDA transparency endpoint
  (https://open.fda.gov). U.S. government works, public domain / CC0; published by FDA with redactions. Product names and
  deficiency topics are parsed by this software from the OCR letter text and may be wrong.
- FDA Orange Book (Approved Drug Products with Therapeutic Equivalence Evaluations) data files, U.S. Food and
  Drug Administration (https://www.fda.gov/media/76860/download). U.S. government work, public domain. Patents are as
  listed by the applicant; FDA does not verify them.
- FDA Purple Book (Database of Licensed Biological Products) monthly data downloads, U.S. Food and Drug Administration
  (https://purplebooksearch.fda.gov/index.cfm?event=downloads). U.S. government work, public domain. Exclusivity dates are
  listed only where FDA has made a determination.
- Health Canada Notice of Compliance Database (https://health-products.canada.ca/api/notice-of-compliance/). Contains
  information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada (https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada).
